{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumUniverses.CategoricalConnectionUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumUniverses.CategoricalConnectionUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.GaugeTheory"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalConnection.unique_up_to_gauge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalConnection.unique_up_to_gauge","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection-unique.lean#L43-L62","doc":"**Uniqueness of categorical connections up to gauge (proved,\nconditional on `Epi fh.mul`).**\n\nTwo `CategoricalConnection C fh` instances with the same 1-form\nobject and the same Leibniz right-hand side (after `eqToHom`\ntransport) have the same connection morphism, provided the\nmultiplication is an epimorphism: the Leibniz rule `μ ≫ ∇ = rhs`\nthen cancels.  This replaces a false\n`Subsingleton (CategoricalConnection C fh)` axiom (free fields\nadmit distinct instances) with the determination the Leibniz rule\ngenuinely provides. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-connection-unique","label":"prop:categorical-connection-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}